  "guide": {
    "intro": [
      "Zen is a school of Mahayana Buddhism that points directly at experience: sit, breathe, work, eat, and see what is already here. It grew from Chinese Chan, which blended Indian Buddhism with Daoist naturalness.",
      "It spread to Korea, Vietnam and Japan, where it shaped tea, gardens, ink painting and archery. Two schools remain central in Japan: Sōtō, which stresses sitting, and Rinzai, which uses koans."
    ],
    "origin": "China, then Japan",
    "era": "6th c. CE to today",
    "figures": [
